The bug: `extract_names` produced "a coffeetable 1" (with article) for some receptacles, so `go to a coffeetable 1` failed; also "a sofa 1" never matched the real "sofa 1". Also it visited the dresser (which contains the creditcards) but never took them because it only took objects in the *current* observation and the residual article prefix broke matching. Fix: normalize receptacle names by stripping articles, and take objects when seen, not just on first pass.

